//! Phase 10.1 — `providers/implementations/encode_decode/decode_der2key.c`: the provider's
//! **DER-to-key decoders** — 69 `OSSL_OP_DECODER` tables published by both the `default` and the
//! `base` provider, generated by one `D2I_PUBKEY_NOCTX`/`MAKE_DECODER` pair over a shared engine.
//!
//! This is the largest of the eleven row-publishing units of `docs/PHASE-10-SUBPHASES.md` §1a
//! (`69 tables`, `138 rows`), and the eighth to land. It is `docs/DECISIONS.md` D436's measured
//! "next slice": its four-helper closure (`ossl_ml_kem_d2i_PKCS8`/`_PUBKEY`,
//! `ossl_ml_dsa_d2i_PKCS8`/`_PUBKEY`, D436's three new modules) is landed, and D435's `nm`
//! measurement showed the rest of its undefined set is landed too.
//!
//! ## The engine is shared, the row is the table
//!
//! `der2key_decode` reads one top-level DER object through `ossl_read_der`, then walks the selection
//! levels — private key, public key, parameters — trying the row's `d2i_PKCS8`/`d2i_private_key`,
//! its `d2i_PUBKEY`/`d2i_public_key` and its `d2i_key_params` in turn, running the row's `check_key`
//! and `adjust_key` on the result and announcing the key to the framework's callback. The
//! `MAKE_DECODER` macro (`decode_der2key.c:1223-1257`) expands once per row into a
//! `keytype_desc_st`, a `newctx`/`does_selection` pair and a dispatch table; the engine is one.
//!
//! ## The dependency closure is landed
//!
//! Every undefined symbol of the authority's own object is a landed crate function: the classical
//! `d2i` backends (`d2i_DHparams`, `d2i_DSAPrivateKey`, `d2i_ECPrivateKey`, `d2i_RSA_PUBKEY`, …,
//! all Phase 8), the SPKI backends (`ossl_d2i_DH_PUBKEY`, …, D369's `crypto/x509/x_pubkey.c`), the
//! PKCS#8 backends (`ossl_dh_key_from_pkcs8`, …), the four D436 codec helpers, and
//! `ossl_slh_dsa_*`. That is why this unit needs no 10.6 hand-off, exactly as D435 measured.
//!
//! ## The bytes are the contract
//!
//! `RT-CODEC` fetches each row by its own name and property through both providers (the identity
//! join) and drives the rows a fixed, published input can reach: the RFC 7748/8032 and RFC 8410
//! `PrivateKeyInfo`/`SubjectPublicKeyInfo` DER the authority's own `evppkey_ecx.txt` carries for the
//! four ECX types, the PKCS#3/X9.42 parameter DER its `20-test_dhparam_data` carries for the two DH
//! parameter rows, and the selection refusals the engine itself raises. A transcription that
//! round-trips its own encoder is not this (`docs/PHASE-10-SUBPHASES.md` §3.1). Rows whose fixed
//! input the probe does not carry are observed at the identity join only and named as such, the same
//! §3.5 rule D434 applied to its `RSA`/`RSA-PSS`/`DSA`/`DHX` text rows.
//!
//! SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

